    "id": "bio16-008",
    "t": "practice",
    "q": "In an F2 generation of 929 pea plants from a monohybrid cross of purple (dominant) and white flowers, how many white-flowered plants would you expect?<br><br><br>A) About 697<br>B) About 464<br>C) About 310<br>D) About 232<br>E) About 929",
    "a": "<b>D) About 232</b><br><br>Segregation gives a 3 : 1 ratio, so 1/4 of the plants are white (homozygous recessive): <i>929/4 = 232</i>. (Mendel observed 224.)"
