    "t": "practice",
    "q": "A region of the nucleus stains darkly and the genes in it are rarely transcribed. What is it?<br><br><br>A) Heterochromatin<br>B) Euchromatin<br>C) The nucleolus<br>D) A plasmid<br>E) A telomere",
    "a": "<b>A) Heterochromatin</b><br><br>Heterochromatin is tightly packed, so RNA polymerase cannot reach the genes, and it is transcriptionally inactive. Euchromatin is loosely packed and active. The inactive X chromosome (Barr body) is an example of heterochromatin."
